From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarred Sumner <jarred@jarredsumner.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:07:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dns(macOS): use DNSServiceQueryRecord so split DNS can fail
 over (#44519)

Fixes #44075. Closes #44449. On macOS, dns.lookup(), fetch() and sockets
now resolve split-DNS names, for example a VPN resolver behind iCloud
Private Relay. getaddrinfo(3) resolves these names, but Bun reported
ENOTFOUND. mDNSResponder asks the next resolver after a negative answer
only when the client sends the failover attribute.
DNSServiceGetAddrInfoEx (#40675) accepts that attribute but never sends
it, and the daemon reads it only for QueryRecord requests. This PR does
what libinfo does: one DNSServiceQueryRecordWithAttribute per family.
macOS 12 falls back to plain DNSServiceQueryRecord on the same code
path. Thanks to @mimi1vx for the diagnosis. Compared with #44449: the
hostname is sent as written (a trailing dot turns off search domains, so
http://intranet/ would stop resolving), a link-local AAAA keeps its
interface scope (fe80::1%7), and removed records are still ignored.
Verified: new tests put a scripted mDNSResponder behind the unix socket
of the daemon and check the requests and the answers. All 10 pass with
bun bd test test/js/bun/dns/. The 9 that existed at that time all fail
on 1.4.3 with USE_SYSTEM_BUN=1, and the tenth was not run there. The
requests are now identical to those of getaddrinfo(3), and 21 lookups
through the real daemon match 1.4.3. Not verified: real failover, which
needs a split-DNS machine. @mimi1vx @sassdavid, can you try this build
with bunx bun-pr?

