From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kushal khemka <kushalkhemka@Kushals-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:39:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Blob, fetch: a Blob made of other Blobs keeps them as parts,
 and fetch sends the parts without joining them

new Blob([blob, blob, ...]) copied every part into one new buffer, and a program that builds a request body
from cached parts (Pi: a 9 MB conversation, one Blob per message) paid that copy, and the page faults of a
fresh 9 MB allocation, on every request. Blobs cannot change, so a Blob made of in-memory Blobs (256 KiB or
more in all) now keeps their stores as parts (StoreSlot); whatever reads its store joins them then, once, so
every other use sees what it saw before. fetch() hands the parts to the HTTP client (HTTPRequestBody::Parts),
which sends them one after the other over HTTP/1.1 (small parts copied together into a 256 KiB buffer for one
write, parts of 64 KiB or more written as they are), with the same Content-Length and bytes. Through a proxy,
with compression or verbose output, or where HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 may be used, the client joins them first.
