From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:49:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] GC timer: no 2-min idle collection without the JIT; drop the
 skip that never fired

The idle full collections came at 10 s, 2 min and 10 min of quiet. A previous commit meant to skip the 2-min one when it
would find the heap as the 10 s one left it, with no code that can age. It never fired: on the built runtime (macOS,
Linux x64 and arm64, default and -jit) full collections still came at 7, 15 and 125 s after an answer. In idle Pi ~35
interpreted CodeBlocks survive the 10 s collection and stay alive, so "no code that can age" was never true, and the
2-min collection found the heap as the first one left it: ~33 M instructions (~14 ms of CPU on an M5), its marking
threads and the allocator's purges after it, for no memory.

An executable compiled ahead of time without the JIT (Pi-Bolt's default build) now defaults to "10,590": 10 s and
10 min of quiet. The code that can age there is interpreted code, which the 10 s collection already lets go of. With the
JIT (the -jit builds, stock Bun) the default stays "10,110,480": optimized code, such as a plugin's DFG/FTL code, ages out
at idle collections only, and keeps aging out at 2 min. BUN_IDLE_GC_SECONDS still overrides both.

The skip (idle_full_finds_nothing) is removed, with the two accessors it used (JSC__VM__totalBytesAllocated,
JSC__VM__hasAgingCode).
---
