From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:25:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] bun_perf (macOS): no os_log at start unless tracing was asked
 for

is_enabled_once() made the Instruments log (os_log_create) at the first
trace() of every process, before it knew whether tracing is on. os_log_create
asks logd for the log's configuration and waits for the answer: 1.2-1.5 M
instructions and 1.6-4.2 ms of wall time on an M5, at every start (the
resolver's first trace(), while the entry module loads). The log is now made
only when BUN_INSTRUMENTS or DYLD_ROOT_PATH asks for tracing; trace() returns
Disabled otherwise, as before.
---
 src/perf/lib.rs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/perf/lib.rs b/src/perf/lib.rs
index 03e41f6957..357d727f64 100644
--- a/src/perf/lib.rs
+++ b/src/perf/lib.rs
@@ -78,7 +78,9 @@ fn is_enabled_once() {
     #[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
     {
         is_enabled_on_mac_os_once();
-        if Darwin::get().is_none() {
+        // Only when tracing was asked for: os_log_create() asks logd for the log's configuration and waits for the answer
+        // (1.5-4 ms of wall time and about 1 M instructions on an M5), which every start paid at its first trace().
+        if IS_ENABLED.load(Ordering::SeqCst) && Darwin::get().is_none() {
             IS_ENABLED.store(false, Ordering::SeqCst);
         }
     }
-- 
